.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-DOWNLOAD-BUCKET 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-download-bucket \- download a bucket's objects to a local directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm download-bucket
.BR \-\-bucket\-ern | \-b
.I ERN
.BR \-\-dir | \-d
.I PATH
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-p\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-recursive\fR|\fB\-r\fR]
[\fB\-\-part\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
[\fB\-\-concurrency\fR|\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-zip\fR|\fB\-z\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads objects from a bucket to a local directory, one file per
object. This is the batch counterpart to
.BR euclid-cli-esm-download-file (1);
each object uses the exact same single-request/multipart logic that
action does, chosen independently per object by its size relative to
.BR \-\-part\-size .
.PP
Objects don't have real parent directories, so
.B \-\-recursive
controls how many of a bucket's keys are treated as "in" it, the same
"delimiter" semantics S3-style listings use to simulate a directory's
immediate contents:
without
.BR \-\-recursive ,
only an object's
.I direct descendants
are downloaded - keys matching
.B \-\-prefix
with no further
.B /
after it. With
.BR \-\-recursive ,
every key matching
.B \-\-prefix
is downloaded, however deeply nested.
.PP
Each downloaded file's local path is
.B \-\-dir
followed by the object's key with
.B \-\-prefix
stripped off the front - e.g. with
.B \-\-prefix
.I archive/
and
.BR \-\-recursive ,
an object keyed
.I archive/2026/report.csv
is written to
.IR <dir>/2026/report.csv ,
creating intermediate directories as needed. Object keys are opaque
strings, not real filesystem paths, so a key that looks absolute (e.g.
.IR /etc/passwd )
is still resolved relative to
.BR \-\-dir ,
not treated as an OS-absolute path; a key containing
.B ..
components is refused rather than written, though, since that would
walk back out of
.B \-\-dir
entirely.
.PP
The full matching object list is fetched (paging through list-objects
as needed) before any download starts. Objects are then downloaded one
at a time, in a deterministic order (sorted by key); within a single
object's multipart download, up to
.B \-\-concurrency
parts still run in parallel, same as
.BR euclid-cli-esm-download-file (1).
Processing continues after a single object fails, so one bad object
doesn't block the rest; the command's own exit status reflects whether
every object succeeded.
.PP
If
.B \-\-zip
is given, once every object has been downloaded,
.BR \-\-dir 's
contents are additionally packed into a single ZIP archive at that
path; the individual files downloaded under
.B \-\-dir
are left in place, so both the loose files and the archive are
available afterwards.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the source bucket. Required.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Local directory to download into. Created (including any missing
parent directories) if it doesn't already exist. Required.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only download objects whose key starts with this prefix, and strip it
from the front of each key to form the local file path. Optional;
empty by default, which matches every object in the bucket.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Download every key matching \fB\-\-prefix\fR, however deeply nested,
instead of only its direct descendants.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-part\-size " " \fIBYTES\fR
Size threshold, in bytes, at or above which an object is fetched as
multipart rather than in a single request - applied per object, same
as
.BR euclid-cli-esm-download-file (1)
\&'s option of the same name. Defaults to \fI5242880\fR (5 MiB), or the
value of \fIeuclid.modules.storage.part-size\fR in the loaded
configuration file if set - see
.BR \-\-config
in
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-concurrency " " \fIN\fR
Number of parts to download in parallel, for any object that goes the
multipart route. Defaults to \fI4\fR, or the value of
\fIeuclid.modules.storage.concurrency\fR in the loaded configuration
file if set; values less than \fI1\fR are treated as \fI1\fR.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zip " " \fIPATH\fR
If given, pack \fB\-\-dir\fR's contents into a single ZIP archive at
this local path once every object has been downloaded. Optional; by
default no archive is created.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every matching object was downloaded (a bucket/prefix combination with
no matching objects is not an error - a warning is printed to standard
error, and an empty JSON array is printed) and, if \fB\-\-zip\fR was
given, the archive was written successfully.
.IP
Without \fB\-\-zip\fR, a JSON array is printed, one entry per object
.RI ( "{key, file, result}" ),
where
.I result
is that object's downloaded file summary (the same shape
.BR euclid-cli-esm-download-file (1)
prints for a single object). With \fB\-\-zip\fR, a JSON object is
printed instead
.RI ( "{objects, zip}" ),
where
.I objects
is that same array and
.I zip
is the archive's path.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, \fB\-\-dir\fR could not be created, one or
more objects failed to download, or (with \fB\-\-zip\fR) the archive
could not be written; the printed JSON still contains one entry per
object, with
.RI ( "{key, file, error: true}" )
in place of
.I result
for each one that failed. Per-object errors, and any ZIP write error,
are also printed to standard error as they happen.
.SH EXAMPLES
Download only the direct contents of a bucket under a prefix:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm download-bucket \e
    --bucket-ern ern:euclid:storage:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --dir ./reports --prefix 2026-08/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Download an entire prefix's tree, with higher per-object part
concurrency:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm download-bucket \e
    --bucket-ern ern:euclid:storage:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --dir ./archive --prefix archive/ --recursive \e
    --part-size 8388608 --concurrency 8
.fi
.RE
.PP
Download a prefix's tree and also pack it into a single archive:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm download-bucket \e
    --bucket-ern ern:euclid:storage:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --dir ./archive --prefix archive/ --recursive \e
    --zip ./archive.zip
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-download-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-directory (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1)
